            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 26-year-old male, admitted on 25/02/2018 with acute right lower quadrant abdominal pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. On admission, physical examination revealed marked rebound tenderness at McBurney's point. Blood tests confirmed leukocytosis with left shift. Abdominal ultrasound supported the diagnosis of acute appendicitis. The patient underwent laparoscopic emergency appendectomy on 26/02/2018 without intraoperative complications. Postoperatively, intravenous antibiotics and analgesics were administered, wound care was performed, and vital signs remained stable throughout. The patient recovered well and was discharged home on 28/02/2018 in good general condition. Patient education regarding wound care and follow-up was provided. Please arrange a follow-up appointment in approximately two weeks.</div>"
            },
